    "title": "Campbell's Fires Executive After Alleged Remarks About Soup Products",
    "text": "• Campbell's has fired Martin Bally, a former vice president, after an investigation into alleged remarks made about the company's soup products.\n• A recording of Bally allegedly described Campbell's products as \"highly process[ed] food\" for \"poor people\" and the chicken as \"bioengineered meat.\"\n• Campbell's confirmed the voice in the recording is believed to be Bally's.\n• Robert Garza, a former cyber security analyst, recorded the conversation and is suing Campbell's.\n• Garza claims Bally made the comments during a meeting about his salary.\n• Garza alleges he was fired after wanting to report Bally's behavior to HR.\n• Campbell's states Garza was terminated for good reason and had been with the company for less than 5 months.\n• Garza is suing for alleged retaliation and a hostile work environment, seeking emotional and economic damages.\n• Campbell's denies the accuracy of the alleged comments and states they do not reflect the company's values.\n• Campbell's says the chicken in its soups comes from USDA-approved suppliers and meets high-quality standards.\n• Campbell's stated it has not been able to verify the validity of the recording and has not been provided with a copy.",
